# A construct the verifier does not represent costs its function alone. The
# function is reported where the construct is, and its JSON record carries its
# verdict, Unresolved with construct.unsupported; every other function is
# verified. A caller relies on the function's contract, which nothing
# establishes (callee.contract); a call of a function whose contract did not
# convert is unsupported where it is; a function that reaches a spec the
# verifier does not represent is not verified.
#
# RUN: not %cpp-verify %S/Inputs/per_function_errors.cpp -- 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TEXT
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --diagnostics-format=json %S/Inputs/per_function_errors.cpp -- 2>/dev/null \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JSON
#
# The same with BMC, and in a Lean export, which exports what it can.
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --backend=bmc --unroll=1 %S/Inputs/per_function_errors.cpp -- 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BMC
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --backend=lean --lean-out=%t.lean %S/Inputs/per_function_errors.cpp -- 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEAN

